## Installed as /etc/audit/audit.rules, loaded at boot by the stock
## auditd.service: ExecStartPost=/sbin/auditctl -R /etc/audit/audit.rules
##
## Arch-agnostic by design: no -F arch= syscall rules. Syscall numbering and name
## availability differ per arch (aarch64 has no chown, 32-bit arm does), and
## auditctl -R stops at the first line it cannot parse, so one arch-wrong line
## takes every later rule down with it.
##
## No `-e 2`: the ruleset stays mutable so a container with cap_add AUDIT_CONTROL
## and pid: host can layer rules at runtime over NETLINK_AUDIT.
##
## Comments must be on their own line — auditctl only honours '#' at column 0;
## a trailing comment parses as arguments.
##
## refs: https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man8/auditctl.8.html
##       https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/audit.rules.7.html

-D
-b 8192
-f 1

## NetworkManager connection profiles: Wi-Fi credentials and connectivity config,
## on the boot partition on every balenaOS device type. A watch on a directory
## covers its subtree, so this catches any profile added, edited or removed.
## The path resolves only once /mnt/boot is mounted; a watch on a nonexistent
## path errors and stops the rest of the load.
-w /mnt/boot/system-connections -p wa -k system_connections
